//
// Transformer-layer device kernels: compile-only gate.
//
// Builds every AIE2P kernel that Phase A of the transformer-layer execution
// studies ports, and checks each object is non-trivial and exports the entry
// points its builder will call. Compiling is not the whole gate -- Peano emits
// a valid, empty object when encoder.cc / addnorm_ffn.cc are built without
// -DBUILD_FFN / -DBUILD_ADDNORM, so compile_kernels.py also enforces a size
// floor and a per-object symbol list.
//
// No NPU is touched: these are Peano object files, not ELFs, and nothing is
// dispatched. That is what makes this suite safe as a PR gate, and it is why
// this test requires only `peano` and not `ryzen_ai_npu2` -- unlike the
// flash_attention and llms lits, which do dispatch.
//
// REQUIRES: peano
//
// RUN: mkdir -p test_npu2_compile_peano
// RUN: cd test_npu2_compile_peano
// RUN: make -f %S/Makefile clean
// RUN: make -f %S/Makefile compile PEANO_INSTALL_DIR=%PEANO_INSTALL_DIR | FileCheck %s
// CHECK: Compilation passed.
